---
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="hero" id="overview" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="hero-topline"><p class="eyebrow">TURBOJ / MACOS / IN DEVELOPMENT</p><span aria-hidden="true">2026</span></div>
    <h1 class="hero-title" id="hero-heading">Java, straight<br class="hero-break" /> to the point.</h1>
    <div class="hero-content">
      <div class="hero-intro">
        <p class="hero-descriptor">The ultra-fast Java editor.</p>
        <p class="hero-question">Remember when writing a program was simple?</p>
        <p class="hero-sequence">Open an editor. Write some code. Compile. Run.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-description">
        <p class="body-copy">TurboJ brings that workflow back to Java, with a classic keyboard-first interface, a built-in compiler workflow, and program output right where you need it.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">No complicated workspace. No unnecessary panels. Just your code.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-bottom">
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={site.links.demo}>See TurboJ in action <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href={site.links.features}>Explore the features <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <p class="hero-tagline">Old-school focus. Modern Java.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
